## Substitute x = 0 into f(x)
f(0) &= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{1}{2}(0)^2}
&= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{0}
&= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}(1)
&= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}
## State the point
The graph meets the $y$-axis at $A\left(0, \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\right)$.
ANSWER: A\left(0, \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\right)

## Write the inequality
The fraction remaining at step $h$ is $\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^h$.
\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^h &< \frac{1}{100}
## Take ln of both sides
\ln\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^h &< \ln\frac{1}{100}
h\ln\left(\frac{3}{4}\right) &< \ln\frac{1}{100}
## Divide by ln(3/4)
$\ln\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)$ is negative, so dividing reverses the inequality.
h &> \frac{\ln\frac{1}{100}}{\ln\frac{3}{4}}
h &> 16.008
## Choose the first whole number
h &= 17
ANSWER: h = 17

## Find the pattern for the perimeter
Each black triangle has half the side length, but there are 3 times as many, so the total perimeter is multiplied by $\frac{3}{2}$ each step.
## Multiply by 3/2 at each step
\text{Step 1: } 3\times\frac{3}{2} &= \frac{9}{2}
\text{Step 2: } \frac{9}{2}\times\frac{3}{2} &= \frac{27}{4}
\text{Step 3: } \frac{27}{4}\times\frac{3}{2} &= \frac{81}{8}
\text{Step 4: } \frac{81}{8}\times\frac{3}{2} &= \frac{243}{16}
ANSWER: 3,\ \tfrac{9}{2},\ \tfrac{27}{4},\ \tfrac{81}{8},\ \tfrac{243}{16}

## Convert each mark to a z-score
Use $z = \frac{x - \mu}{\sigma}$ to compare marks across exams.
z_{\text{Maths}} &= \frac{65 - 70}{15}
&= \frac{-5}{15}
&= -\frac{1}{3}
## Do the same for English
z_{\text{English}} &= \frac{68 - 72}{10}
&= \frac{-4}{10}
&= -\frac{2}{5}
## Compare the z-scores
A higher z-score means Mary is further above the class average. $-0.33$ is bigger than $-0.4$.
-\frac{1}{3} &> -\frac{2}{5}
So Mary did better in Maths, because her z-score there is higher (closer to the mean).
ANSWER: \text{Maths, since } -\frac{1}{3} > -\frac{2}{5}
